sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch05-25> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "The normal form of decapod crustacean sperm-cells is one of many intermediate phases of shrinkage from a spherical form, caused by osmotic withdrawal of fluid without a matching reduction of surface area, so that equivalent shapes are produced by salt solutions of equivalent (molecular-weight-proportional) concentration.";
    dc:type "mechanism";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Decapod sperm-cell shape is an intermediate phase of osmotic shrinkage";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter V, “The Forms of Cells”; topic “Osmotic shapes of sperm-cells”. Scope: sperm-cells of decapod crustacea (Inachus, Galathea, Dromia, crayfish) and, by comparison, red blood cells"
}
